        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "15ed843f-03a9-5116-bab1-94cec8dfea2b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Gangkhar Puensum, Jongsong Peak, Bhutan, Kangchenjunga, Shangri-La\n- Products: Killer Mountain\n- Concepts: mountain elevation, mountain prominence, unclimbed mountains, expedition rescue\n- Topics: mountaineering, sci-fi film plots\n\nFacts:\n- Gangkhar Puensum is the highest mountain in Bhutan.\n- Gangkhar Puensum has an elevation of 7,570 meters and a prominence of 2,995 meters.\n- Gangkhar Puensum is a strong candidate for the highest unclimbed mountain in the world.\n- Jongsong Peak has an elevation of 7,462 meters and is the 57th highest peak in the world.\n- Kangchenjunga is the world’s 3rd highest mountain and lies 20 kilometers south of Jongsong Peak.\n- The sci-fi film Killer Mountain follows climbers sent to rescue a missing expedition from Gangkhar Puensum.\n- In Killer Mountain, the climbers discover the legendary Shangri-La and a creature called the Druk that protects it.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
